0..77 Comment "// Each rule\'s cell counts how many times its right side writes each hole its"
78..157 Comment "// left side binds: the hole\'s Lipschitz constant under the step, the factor by"
158..232 Comment "// which one step can stretch a distance between two instances of the hole"
233..311 Comment "// (Gavazzo and Di Florio, _Quantitative and Metric Rewriting_, 2022, § 8.2)."
312..391 Comment "// `gandr cells` reports the counts of every cell (#2788). `mirror` writes each"
392..470 Comment "// subshrub once and is strictly linear; `left` drops `r`, a constant of zero;"
471..544 Comment "// `twice` and `thrice` write `t` two and three times, so their steps are"
545..596 Comment "// duplicating. A count is reported, never refused."
598..672 Comment "/// Binary shrubs, with operations writing a subshrub zero to three times."
673..675 Other "@["
676..686 Other "normalizes"
686..687 Other "("
